{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ML-09 — Validation and Research Claim Audit\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook audits the Week-5 model using an honest client-grouped split, checks for leakage, reviews real model errors, and rewrites the final claim in careful decision-support language.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Note: if the warehouse label is unavailable, `trend_direction == 'down'` is used only as an evaluation-only proxy. It is never included as a feature."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Two paper findings + my methodology questions\n",
    "\n",
    "**Finding 1 — Content lifecycle / age.** The FlyRank report observes that growing pages were younger on average (about 185 days) than declining pages (about 228 days), while word count was nearly the same at roughly 1.5K words. My methodology question: could client/site mix, topic, historical visibility, or update history explain part of this association? I would treat age as an observed signal rather than evidence that age itself causes decline.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Finding 2 — Freshness multiplier.** The report observes a 5.43:1 growth-to-decline ratio in the 31–90 day freshness window and separately reports a large difference between refreshed and stale pages in the 365+ cohort. It also notes that the 361+ bucket contains only 21 declining pages, so that bucket is unstable. My methodology question: were refreshed and stale pages comparable before the refresh, or could selection effects explain part of the difference? A stronger validation design would control for baseline performance, client/site mix, and pre-refresh characteristics before interpreting the result.\n",
    "\n",
    "These findings are useful as directional observations, but they do not by themselves establish causality."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Setup and data loading\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import subprocess, sys\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, GroupShuffleSplit\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import recall_score, precision_score, f1_score, roc_auc_score, confusion_matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "repo_root = Path('/content/ml-internship-2026')\n",
    "if not repo_root.exists():\n",
    "    subprocess.run(['git', 'clone', 'https://github.com/engyusufayman06/ml-internship-2026.git', str(repo_root)], check=True)\n",
    "data_path = repo_root / 'data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv'\n",
    "if not data_path.exists():\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(f'Missing dataset: {data_path}. Make sure the warehouse data is available.')\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(data_path)\n",
    "print('Shape:', df.shape)\n",
    "print('Columns:', len(df.columns))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Label and feature definition\n",
    "target = 'is_declining_label'\n",
    "if target not in df.columns:\n",
    "    if 'trend_direction' not in df.columns:\n",
    "        raise KeyError('Neither is_declining_label nor trend_direction is available.')\n",
    "    df[target] = (df['trend_direction'].astype(str).str.lower() == 'down').astype(int)\n",
    "    print('Using trend_direction==down as an evaluation-only proxy label.')\n",
    "\n",
    "forbidden = {target, 'trend_direction', 'trend_pct', 'content_id', 'client_id',\n",
    "             'score', 'reason_code', 'action_label', 'freshness_bucket', 'volume_bucket'}\n",
    "features = [c for c in df.columns if c not in forbidden]\n",
    "X = df[features].copy()\n",
    "y = df[target].astype(int)\n",
    "groups = df['client_id'].astype(str)\n",
    "\n",
    "numeric_features = X.select_dtypes(include=np.number).columns.tolist()\n",
    "categorical_features = [c for c in X.columns if c not in numeric_features]\n",
    "\n",
    "numeric_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
    "    ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median', add_indicator=True)),\n",
    "    ('scaler', StandardScaler())\n",
    "])\n",
    "categorical_pipe = Pipeline([\n",
    "    ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')),\n",
    "    ('onehot', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'))\n",
    "])\n",
    "preprocess = ColumnTransformer([\n",
    "    ('num', numeric_pipe, numeric_features),\n",
    "    ('cat', categorical_pipe, categorical_features)\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_model():\n",
    "    return Pipeline([\n",
    "        ('prep', preprocess),\n",
    "        ('model', LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, class_weight='balanced', random_state=42))\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Feature count:', len(features))\n",
    "print('Numeric:', len(numeric_features), '| Categorical:', len(categorical_features))\n",
    "print('Positive rate:', round(y.mean(), 4))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. My model under an honest split (before/after)\n",
    "\n",
    "The **before** result uses a conventional random 80/20 split. The **after** result uses `GroupShuffleSplit` by `client_id`, so a client cannot appear in both train and test. The model, features, preprocessing, seed, and evaluation metrics stay the same. This makes the split design the main change being audited."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def precision_at_k(y_true, scores, k):\n",
    "    k = min(k, len(y_true))\n",
    "    order = np.argsort(-np.asarray(scores))[:k]\n",
    "    return float(np.asarray(y_true)[order].mean()) if k else np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "def evaluate_split(train_idx, test_idx, name):\n",
    "    model = make_model()\n",
    "    model.fit(X.iloc[train_idx], y.iloc[train_idx])\n",
    "    prob = model.predict_proba(X.iloc[test_idx])[:, 1]\n",
    "    pred = (prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "    yt = y.iloc[test_idx].to_numpy()\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        'split': name,\n",
    "        'Recall': recall_score(yt, pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "        'Precision': precision_score(yt, pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "        'F1': f1_score(yt, pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "        'ROC-AUC': roc_auc_score(yt, prob),\n",
    "        'Precision@20': precision_at_k(yt, prob, 20),\n",
    "        'Precision@50': precision_at_k(yt, prob, 50),\n",
    "        '_model': model, '_prob': prob, '_pred': pred, '_test_idx': np.asarray(test_idx)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "all_idx = np.arange(len(df))\n",
    "train_random, test_random = train_test_split(all_idx, test_size=0.20, random_state=42, stratify=y)\n",
    "gss = GroupShuffleSplit(n_splits=1, test_size=0.20, random_state=42)\n",
    "train_group, test_group = next(gss.split(X, y, groups=groups))\n",
    "\n",
    "before = evaluate_split(train_random, test_random, 'Before: random 80/20')\n",
    "after = evaluate_split(train_group, test_group, 'After: client-grouped 80/20')\n",
    "results = pd.DataFrame([{k:v for k,v in before.items() if not k.startswith('_')},\n",
    "                        {k:v for k,v in after.items() if not k.startswith('_')}])\n",
    "print(results.to_string(index=False, float_format=lambda x: f'{x:.4f}'))\n",\    "\n",
    "random_overlap = set(groups.iloc[train_random]) & set(groups.iloc[test_random])\n",
    "group_overlap = set(groups.iloc[train_group]) & set(groups.iloc[test_group])\n",
    "print('Random split client overlap:', len(random_overlap))\n",
    "print('Grouped split client overlap:', len(group_overlap))\n",
    "assert len(group_overlap) == 0, 'Grouped split has client overlap.'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Apply the Week-4 baseline to the exact same grouped test rows for context.\n",
    "test_df = df.iloc[test_group].copy()\n",
    "baseline_flag = (test_df['days_since_last_update'] >= 180) & (test_df['impressions_90d'] >= 3000)\n",
    "baseline_pred = baseline_flag.astype(int).to_numpy()\n",
    "yt = y.iloc[test_group].to_numpy()\n",
    "baseline_score = test_df['impressions_90d'].where(baseline_flag, 0).to_numpy()\n",
    "baseline_row = {\n",
    "    'split': 'W04 baseline on grouped test',\n",
    "    'Recall': recall_score(yt, baseline_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "    'Precision': precision_score(yt, baseline_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "    'F1': f1_score(yt, baseline_pred, zero_division=0),\n",
    "    'ROC-AUC': roc_auc_score(yt, baseline_score) if len(np.unique(yt)) > 1 else np.nan,\n",
    "    'Precision@20': precision_at_k(yt, baseline_score, 20),\n",
    "    'Precision@50': precision_at_k(yt, baseline_score, 50)\n",
    "}\n",
    "print(pd.DataFrame([baseline_row, {k:v for k,v in after.items() if not k.startswith('_')}]).to_string(index=False, float_format=lambda x: f'{x:.4f}'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Leakage audit\n",
    "\n",
    "The final feature set excludes the target, the fields used to derive the target (`trend_direction`, `trend_pct`), identifiers, and fields produced by the Week-4 decision rule. This keeps target information and downstream rule outputs out of the learned feature space."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "leakage_fields = ['is_declining_label', 'trend_direction', 'trend_pct', 'content_id', 'client_id',\n",
    "                  'score', 'reason_code', 'action_label', 'freshness_bucket', 'volume_bucket']\n",
    "leakage_audit = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'field': leakage_fields,\n",
    "    'present_in_data': [f in df.columns for f in leakage_fields],\n",
    "    'used_as_feature': [f in features for f in leakage_fields]\n",
    "})\n",
    "print(leakage_audit.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "assert not leakage_audit['used_as_feature'].any(), 'Potential leakage field entered the feature set.'\n",
    "print('LEAKAGE AUDIT PASSED')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Real failure examples\n",
    "\n",
    "The examples below are from the grouped holdout. IDs are pseudonymized; only safe analytical fields are shown. False negatives are declining pages the model missed, while false positives are pages the model flagged that were not labeled declining."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "err = test_df.copy()\n",
    "err['actual'] = yt\n",
    "err['predicted'] = after['_pred']\n",
    "err['probability'] = after['_prob']\n",
    "safe_cols = [c for c in ['content_id','client_id','content_type','days_since_last_update','impressions_90d','trend_pct'] if c in err.columns]\n",
    "fn = err[(err.actual == 1) & (err.predicted == 0)].sort_values('probability').head(3)\n",
    "fp = err[(err.actual == 0) & (err.predicted == 1)].sort_values('probability', ascending=False).head(3)\n",
    "print('FALSE NEGATIVES')\n",
    "print(fn[safe_cols + ['actual','predicted','probability']].to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print('\\nFALSE POSITIVES')\n",
    "print(fp[safe_cols + ['actual','predicted','probability']].to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print('\\nConfusion matrix [rows=actual, cols=predicted]:')\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(yt, after['_pred']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Inspect strongest learned coefficients as an explainability check.\n",
    "model = after['_model']\n",
    "feature_names = model.named_steps['prep'].get_feature_names_out()\n",
    "coefs = model.named_steps['model'].coef_[0]\n",
    "coef_df = pd.DataFrame({'feature': feature_names, 'coefficient': coefs})\n",
    "print('Top positive coefficients:')\n",
    "print(coef_df.nlargest(10, 'coefficient').to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print('\\nTop negative coefficients:')\n",
    "print(coef_df.nsmallest(10, 'coefficient').to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Claim rewrite\n",
    "\n",
    "**Too strong:** “The Logistic Regression model accurately identifies declining content and can improve the content-refresh process.”\n",
    "\n",
    "**Rewritten claim:** “On the evaluated client-grouped holdout, Logistic Regression produced measured recall, precision, F1, ROC-AUC, and Precision@K results. These results provide directional evidence that the available signals can support a review-prioritization workflow; they do not establish causality or guarantee performance on future clients or time periods.”\n",
    "\n",
    "**Operational interpretation:** the model is decision-support for human review, not an automatic decision-maker."
   ]
  },
  {
